<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		ReGrowth: Boiling: extra wild animal spawns in RG_BoilingForest from other animal mods.
		This folder only loads with ReGrowth: Boiling (see loadFolders.xml). The first block's Mythic Ages entries carry their
		own MayRequire; every other block is gated on its animal mod, and each block is its own operation so one failing
		cannot stop the rest.
		From Too Many Mods' ReGrowthBoiling.xml, where it had no setting. Dropped from it (2026-10-13): the Alpha Mythology block
		(that mod never got a 1.6 build), and the commonality changes to the biome's own animals that rode along with the
		Alpha Animals and VAE blocks (owlbeast up; squirrel, hare, rat, raccoon, deer, alpaca and elk down). Those added no
		animal: the number of wild animals comes from the biome's animal density, not from the sum of commonalities, so the
		added animals need no room made for them.
		Why the checks matter: a biome that lists a pawn kind that does not exist, or gets the same animal twice (here and in
		the animal's own wildBiomes or another mod's patch), throws when it builds its commonality table
		(BiomeDef.CommonalityOfAnimal), which breaks wild animal spawning in that biome.
		Audited 2026-10-13 (analysis/regrowth_audit.py) against the installed 1.6 mods: every Alpha Animals, Megafauna,
		Vanilla Animals Expanded, Mythic Ages and Dark Ages pawn kind exists, none is already in the biome's own list or lists
		the biome in its race's wildBiomes, no installed mod patches any of them in, and no animal appears twice in this file.
		Not installed here, checked from other sources instead: Dinosauria (spincrus.dinosauria) has no public source. All
		its names match the race defNames that Combat Extended's and Alpha Biomes' Dinosauria patches target; that its pawn
		kinds share those names and that none already lists this biome is unconfirmed.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RG_BoilingForest"]/wildAnimals</xpath>
		<value>
			<MA_Hellboar MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.08</MA_Hellboar>
			<MA_Scarodon MayRequire="veterano.mythicages.megafaunabestiary">0.1</MA_Scarodon>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
